      "result": "All 19 checklist items have been executed and recorded — **14 PASS, 5 FAIL**.\n\nThe core happy paths work well: posting jobs, browsing, search, filtering, applying, and the employer dashboard with per-job application lists and delete confirmation.\n\nThe five failures:\n\n| ID | Issue |\n|---|---|\n| **FT-18** | Job editing is entirely unimplemented — no edit control on the dashboard or details page, and candidate edit routes return 404. |\n| **CS-10** | Business validation missing: a job published with zero required skills, and another published with min salary 150000 > max 50000 (rendered as \"$150k - $50k\"). Only native HTML5 required-field checks exist. |\n| **CS-11** | Duplicate applications allowed — the same email applied twice to the same job, creating two records with a success toast both times. |\n| **IX-19** | No persistence — created jobs vanish on reload; localStorage is empty. |\n| **CT-20** | Off-by-one date formatting — jobs and applications created today display \"Yesterday\". |\n\nTwo secondary observations worth noting, though they didn't fail their items: the employer dashboard for Sarah Chen (TechCorp Solutions) also lists jobs publicly attributed to other companies (BrandForward Agency, ContentHub, CloudScale Inc), letting her delete them; and the annual salary of the skill-less test job rendered as \"$90000 - $130000/hr\" — unformatted and incorrectly suffixed with \"/hr\".",
